<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed all three direct sales of paper and four repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 2.130 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    1 year     22.65 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    6 months   21.59 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    90 days    21.33 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     39 days   21.49 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     31 days   21.25 pct</p>
<p>    550 million     13 days   21.48 pct</p>
<p>    130 million	3 days   20.25 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
